{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Rock that begot you — you abandon.</b> The prophet speaks and wonders how you forgot the one who begot you and served new things. Also this: \"Rock that begot you\" is like \"Look unto the rock whence you were hewn\" (Isaiah 51:1) — as though from Him it was, for everything is by the might of HaShem, like \"I stretch out the earth\" (Isaiah 42:5). The wonder of those with warped hearts is on account of \"I this day have begotten you\" (Psalms 2:7) — and they forgot this verse." "<b>תשי</b> — like לא תנשה. And the hidden [letter] after the tav is in place of the dagesh, which is an alef quiescent [אלף הבלוע], and the yod in place of the heh. And likewise אל תמחי — both mil'el, to distinguish between masculine and feminine in verbs whose final letter is a weak heh. And the correct in my eyes is that the yod is added, and it is according to the pattern of אל תט — the sayings of my mouth." "<b>מחוללך.</b> Like ילדך. And behold, El, who is mighty and strong, is like Rock. And it is possible that the form of מחוללך is from מחיל, like \"pregnant, about to give birth\" — the beginning [תחיל]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:00.758482358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}